/* Short study summaries of every surah, written for this site as a learning aid.
   They are a guide to what each surah contains, not a translation or tafsir.
   Format: number: [theme, [icon, title, text], ...]   (verse numbers in brackets) */
window.SURAH_SUMMARY = {
  1: ["The opening prayer of the Quran, recited in every rak‘ah. It is a conversation between the servant and Allah.",
    ["book", "Praise", "All praise belongs to Allah, Lord of all the worlds, the Most Compassionate, the Most Merciful, Master of the Day of Judgement (1–4)."],
    ["heart", "Promise", "You alone we worship, and You alone we ask for help (5)."],
    ["path", "Request", "Guide us on the straight path — the path of those You have blessed, not of those who earned anger nor of those who went astray (6–7)."]],
  2: ["The longest surah. It builds a community of faith: who believes, lessons from earlier nations, and laws for daily life.",
    ["book", "Three kinds of people", "The Quran is guidance for the God-conscious. People are described as believers, deniers, and hypocrites who say one thing and hide another (1–20)."],
    ["garden", "Adam in the Garden", "Allah places Adam on earth as a khalīfah (successor) and teaches him the names. The angels bow; Iblis refuses out of pride. Adam and his wife slip, repent, and are forgiven (30–39)."],
    ["sea", "The Children of Israel", "They are reminded of Allah’s favours: rescue from Pharaoh, the sea parted, food from heaven, twelve springs from a rock — and of how they broke their promises and worshipped the calf (40–103)."],
    ["scales", "The cow", "Told to sacrifice a cow, they kept asking for more and more details and nearly did not do it. The surah is named after this story (67–73)."],
    ["kaaba", "Ibrahim and the Ka‘bah", "Ibrahim and Isma‘il raise the House and pray for a messenger from their children. The direction of prayer is changed from Jerusalem to the Ka‘bah (124–150)."],
    ["scales", "Laws for life", "Fasting in Ramadan, hajj, charity, marriage and divorce, wine and gambling, care of orphans, the ban on interest, and writing down debts — the longest verse of the Quran (177–283)."],
    ["shield", "Talut and Jalut", "A small, patient army under Talut defeats a huge one by Allah’s permission, and young Dawud kills Jalut (246–251)."],
    ["throne", "Ayat al-Kursi", "The greatest verse: Allah, the Ever-Living, whom neither drowsiness nor sleep overtakes; His Kursi extends over the heavens and the earth (255). There is no compulsion in religion (256)."],
    ["sprout", "Life after death", "Ibrahim asks to see how the dead are raised, and a man is made to die for a hundred years and then brought back (258–260)."],
    ["heart", "The closing prayer", "The Messenger and the believers believe in all the prophets. Allah does not burden a soul beyond what it can bear (285–286)."]],
  3: ["Steadfast faith: the family of ‘Imran, a dialogue with the People of the Book, and the lessons of the battle of Uhud.",
    ["book", "The Book", "The Quran confirms the Torah and the Gospel. Some verses are clear and decisive, others are open to interpretation; the firm in knowledge say, ‘We believe in it all’ (1–9)."],
    ["mosque", "Maryam, Zakariyya and ‘Isa", "Maryam’s mother dedicates her to Allah. Zakariyya looks after her and is given Yahya in old age. Angels give Maryam the news of ‘Isa, who speaks as a baby and, by Allah’s permission, heals the sick; he calls his disciples (33–63)."],
    ["rope", "Hold together", "Hold firmly to the rope of Allah, all together, and do not be divided. You are the best community when you enjoin good and forbid wrong (102–110)."],
    ["shield", "Badr and Uhud", "Allah helped the believers at Badr. At Uhud the archers left their post and victory turned to hardship — a lesson in obedience, patience and trust (121–175)."],
    ["sky", "People of understanding", "In the creation of the heavens and the earth are signs. Those who remember Allah standing, sitting and lying down make a beautiful prayer (190–200)."]],
  4: ["Justice in the family and in society, with special care for women, orphans and the weak.",
    ["scales", "Orphans and inheritance", "Guard the property of orphans, give women their dowries, and divide inheritance by fixed shares (1–14)."],
    ["house", "Family life", "Marriage, kind treatment, settling disputes between spouses, and standing firm for justice even against yourself or your family (19–35, 135)."],
    ["shield", "Hypocrites and struggle", "Obey Allah and the Messenger, fight for the oppressed, shorten the prayer in danger, and beware of those who waver between two sides (59–146)."],
    ["book", "The People of the Book", "They did not kill ‘Isa nor crucify him; Allah raised him. ‘Isa is a messenger of Allah — do not say ‘Three’ (153–171)."]],
  5: ["Keep your promises. Rules of food, purity and justice, and the story of the table sent down for ‘Isa’s disciples.",
    ["scales", "Promises and what is lawful", "Fulfil your contracts. Lawful and unlawful food, how to make wudu and tayammum, and be just even to people you dislike (1–11)."],
    ["book", "The religion completed", "‘Today I have perfected your religion for you, completed My favour upon you, and chosen Islam as your religion’ (3)."],
    ["mountain", "The holy land", "Musa’s people refuse to enter the land out of fear, so they wander in the wilderness for forty years (20–26)."],
    ["path", "The two sons of Adam", "One brother kills the other out of envy, then learns how to bury him. Whoever kills one soul unjustly, it is as if he killed all mankind (27–32)."],
    ["table", "The table from heaven", "The disciples ask ‘Isa for a table spread with food from heaven, and Allah sends it as a sign (112–115). On the Last Day ‘Isa will say he only told people to worship Allah (116–120)."]],
  6: ["A powerful call to worship Allah alone, answering idol-worship with signs from creation.",
    ["sky", "Signs of the Creator", "Allah made the heavens, the earth, darkness and light. With Him are the keys of the unseen; not a leaf falls without His knowledge (1–73)."],
    ["sky", "Ibrahim and the stars", "Ibrahim looks at a star, then the moon, then the sun. Each one sets, and he says, ‘I do not love things that set,’ and turns to the One who created them (74–83)."],
    ["book", "The line of prophets", "Eighteen prophets are named, from Nuh to ‘Isa — ‘so follow their guidance’ (84–90)."],
    ["scales", "The straight path", "False customs about cattle and crops are rejected. Then come the great commands: no partners with Allah, kindness to parents, no killing, justice in measure and speech (136–153)."]],
  7: ["The long struggle between truth and falsehood, from Adam through the prophets to Musa.",
    ["garden", "Adam and Iblis", "Iblis refuses to bow, saying ‘I am better than him.’ He whispers to Adam and his wife until they eat from the tree. They repent; the best clothing is God-consciousness (11–27)."],
    ["wall", "The people of the Heights", "Men on the heights between Paradise and the Fire recognise both groups and hope for mercy (46–49)."],
    ["ship", "Five warning stories", "Nuh and the flood, Hud and ‘Ad, Salih and Thamud with the she-camel, Lut, and Shu‘ayb of Madyan — each people rejected their prophet and was destroyed (59–93)."],
    ["staff", "Musa and Pharaoh", "The staff, the magicians who believe, the plagues, the sea crossing, Musa on the mountain, the tablets, and the golden calf (103–171)."],
    ["heart", "The first promise", "Allah asked all the children of Adam, ‘Am I not your Lord?’ and they said, ‘Yes, we testify’ (172)."]],
  8: ["Lessons after the battle of Badr, the first great battle of Islam.",
    ["heart", "True believers", "Their hearts tremble when Allah is mentioned, and their faith grows when His verses are recited (2–4)."],
    ["shield", "The day of Badr", "A small group faced a large army. Allah sent angels, rain and calm, and gave them victory (5–19, 41–48)."],
    ["coins", "Spoils and unity", "The spoils belong to Allah and the Messenger, with a fifth for the needy. Obey, do not quarrel, and be patient (1, 41, 46)."]],
  9: ["The only surah without ‘Bismillah’. It ends treaties that were broken and exposes hypocrisy at the time of Tabuk.",
    ["scroll", "The declaration", "Treaties with those who broke them are ended after four months; those who kept their word are honoured (1–15)."],
    ["cave", "The cave", "During the hijrah the Prophet ﷺ tells his companion in the cave, ‘Do not grieve; Allah is with us’ (40)."],
    ["shield", "Hunayn and Tabuk", "Numbers did not help at Hunayn until Allah sent calm. On the hard journey to Tabuk the hypocrites made excuses to stay home (25–27, 38–96)."],
    ["coins", "Who receives zakah", "Eight groups are named: the poor, the needy, and others (60)."],
    ["mosque", "Two mosques", "A mosque built to cause harm, and a mosque founded on God-consciousness from the first day (107–110)."],
    ["heart", "The three who stayed behind", "Three sincere men who missed Tabuk were left alone until the earth felt narrow; then Allah accepted their repentance (117–118)."]],
  10: ["Allah’s signs and mercy; revelation is true, and faith must come before it is too late.",
    ["sky", "Signs and mercy", "The sun and moon, day and night, and safety on the sea all point to Allah. People call on Him in danger and forget Him in ease (1–36)."],
    ["ship", "Nuh and Musa", "Nuh trusts Allah before his people. Pharaoh believes only as he is drowning — too late; his body is kept as a sign (71–92)."],
    ["heart", "The people of Yunus", "They alone believed when the punishment came near, and Allah removed it from them (98)."]],
  11: ["Seven prophets, seven peoples — and the command to stay upright.",
    ["ship", "Nuh and the ark", "Nuh builds the ark while his people mock. His own son refuses to come aboard and drowns. The ark rests on Mount Judi (25–49)."],
    ["wind", "Hud and Salih", "‘Ad rejects Hud; Thamud kills the she-camel sent as a sign to Salih (50–68)."],
    ["house", "Ibrahim’s guests and Lut", "Angels bring Ibrahim news of a son, then go to Lut, whose city is turned upside down (69–83)."],
    ["scales", "Shu‘ayb", "He tells Madyan to give full measure and weight and not to cheat people (84–95)."],
    ["path", "Stay upright", "‘So remain steadfast as you have been commanded,’ and establish prayer at the two ends of the day (112–115)."]],
  12: ["The most beautiful of stories — the whole life of Yusuf told in one surah.",
    ["sky", "The dream", "Young Yusuf sees eleven stars, the sun and the moon bowing to him. His father Ya‘qub tells him to keep it from his brothers (4–6)."],
    ["well", "The well", "His jealous brothers throw him into a well and tell their father a false story. A caravan finds him and sells him in Egypt (7–20)."],
    ["house", "The test in the house", "The wife of the minister tries to tempt him. He refuses, saying ‘I seek refuge in Allah,’ and prefers prison to sin (23–35)."],
    ["night", "Prison and the king’s dream", "He explains the dreams of two prisoners, and later the king’s dream of seven fat and seven lean cows — seven good years, then seven of famine (36–49)."],
    ["coins", "In charge of the storehouses", "Proved innocent, he is put in charge of Egypt’s grain. His brothers come for food and do not recognise him (50–87)."],
    ["heart", "The family reunited", "He forgives his brothers. His shirt restores Ya‘qub’s sight, the family comes to Egypt, and the dream comes true (88–101)."]],
  13: ["Truth is like water that stays; falsehood is like foam that vanishes.",
    ["rain", "Thunder and rain", "The thunder glorifies Him with praise. Rain fills the valleys; the foam disappears while what benefits people remains (12–17)."],
    ["heart", "Hearts at rest", "‘Surely in the remembrance of Allah do hearts find rest’ (28). Allah does not change a people’s condition until they change what is in themselves (11)."]],
  14: ["Gratitude and ingratitude, and the prayer of Ibrahim for Makkah.",
    ["heart", "Be grateful", "‘If you are grateful, I will surely give you more’ (7)."],
    ["fire", "Shaytan’s speech", "On the Last Day Shaytan says, ‘I only called you and you answered me — do not blame me, blame yourselves’ (22)."],
    ["tree", "The good word", "A good word is like a good tree with firm roots and branches in the sky; a bad word is like a tree torn out of the ground (24–26)."],
    ["kaaba", "Ibrahim’s prayer", "‘My Lord, make this city safe… I have settled some of my family in a valley without crops near Your Sacred House’ (35–41)."]],
  15: ["Allah protects His message; the story of Iblis and of destroyed towns.",
    ["book", "The guarded Book", "‘We sent down the Reminder, and We will surely guard it’ (9)."],
    ["garden", "Adam and Iblis", "Man is made from clay; Iblis refuses to bow and is given time until the Day (26–44)."],
    ["ruins", "Lut and the people of al-Hijr", "Angels visit Ibrahim, then Lut. The people of al-Hijr carved houses in the mountains but were not saved (51–84)."]],
  16: ["A surah of blessings — and the bee as a sign for people who think.",
    ["rain", "Countless blessings", "Cattle, rain, crops, the sea, the stars for finding the way: ‘If you tried to count Allah’s blessings you could never number them’ (3–18)."],
    ["hive", "The bee", "Your Lord inspired the bee to build homes in mountains and trees; from it comes a drink of many colours in which there is healing (68–69)."],
    ["scales", "The most complete command", "Allah commands justice, excellence and giving to relatives, and forbids indecency, wrong and oppression (90)."],
    ["heart", "Ibrahim and the way of wisdom", "Ibrahim was a whole nation in himself. ‘Call to the way of your Lord with wisdom and good advice’ (120–125)."]],
  17: ["The Night Journey, and a set of commandments for a good life.",
    ["mosque", "The Night Journey", "Glory to the One who took His servant by night from the Sacred Mosque to the Farthest Mosque (1)."],
    ["scales", "The commandments", "Worship none but Allah, be gentle with parents, give relatives their due, do not waste, do not kill, stay away from adultery, guard the orphan’s property, weigh fairly, and do not walk proudly (23–39)."],
    ["garden", "Adam and Iblis", "Iblis promises to mislead Adam’s children, but has no power over Allah’s true servants (61–65)."],
    ["book", "The Quran", "It is healing and mercy. If all humans and jinn gathered they could not produce its like (82–88)."]],
  18: ["Four stories about four trials: faith, wealth, knowledge and power. Recommended to recite on Fridays.",
    ["cave", "The people of the cave", "Young believers flee to a cave to protect their faith. Allah makes them sleep for three hundred and nine years, then wakes them as a sign (9–26)."],
    ["garden", "The man with two gardens", "A rich man boasts of his gardens and doubts the Hour. His gardens are destroyed, and he is left wringing his hands (32–44)."],
    ["ship", "Musa and al-Khidr", "Musa travels to learn from a servant of Allah who damages a boat, takes the life of a boy, and repairs a wall — each with a hidden wisdom (60–82)."],
    ["wall", "Dhul-Qarnayn", "A just king travels west and east, then builds a barrier of iron and copper to protect a people from Ya’juj and Ma’juj (83–98)."]],
  19: ["Mercy to the prophets and their families, told in gentle words.",
    ["heart", "Zakariyya’s prayer", "Old and with white hair, he calls his Lord quietly and is given a son, Yahya (2–15)."],
    ["palm", "Maryam and ‘Isa", "An angel brings Maryam news of a pure son. She gives birth beneath a palm tree, and the baby ‘Isa speaks from the cradle: ‘I am the servant of Allah’ (16–36)."],
    ["house", "Ibrahim and his father", "Ibrahim calls his father gently — ‘O my dear father’ — away from idols (41–50)."],
    ["book", "More prophets", "Musa, Isma‘il and Idris are remembered; when the verses of the Most Merciful were recited to them they fell down in prostration, weeping (51–58)."]],
  20: ["The story of Musa, told to comfort the Prophet ﷺ: ‘We did not send down the Quran to distress you.’",
    ["fire", "The fire in the valley", "Musa sees a fire and is called in the sacred valley of Tuwa. He is given the staff and the shining hand and asks, ‘My Lord, open my chest for me’ (9–36)."],
    ["river", "The baby in the river", "His mother was inspired to place him in a chest on the river; he grew up under Allah’s eye (37–40)."],
    ["staff", "Pharaoh and the magicians", "The magicians’ ropes seem to move, but Musa’s staff swallows them all. The magicians believe at once (56–76)."],
    ["mountain", "The sea and the calf", "The sea opens a dry path. While Musa is on the mountain, the Samiri makes a calf for the people (77–98)."],
    ["garden", "Adam forgot", "Adam was warned about Shaytan but forgot; then his Lord chose him, forgave him and guided him (115–123)."]],
  21: ["The prophets, one after another — all called to the same Lord, and all were answered.",
    ["sky", "Signs in creation", "The heavens and earth were one mass and were split apart, and every living thing was made from water (30–33)."],
    ["fire", "Ibrahim and the idols", "Ibrahim breaks the idols and is thrown into a fire. Allah says, ‘O fire, be cool and safe for Ibrahim’ (51–70)."],
    ["book", "Prayers answered", "Nuh, Dawud and Sulayman, Ayyub in his illness, Yunus in the darkness — ‘There is no god but You; glory be to You; I was among the wrongdoers’ — and Zakariyya (76–90)."],
    ["heart", "A mercy to the worlds", "‘We have not sent you except as a mercy to all the worlds’ (107)."]],
  22: ["The Hour, the pilgrimage, and striving for Allah.",
    ["quake", "The shaking of the Hour", "The earthquake of the Hour is a tremendous thing; every nursing mother will forget her child (1–2)."],
    ["sprout", "Proof of resurrection", "Man was made from dust, then a drop; and the dead earth stirs and grows when rain falls on it (5–7)."],
    ["kaaba", "The pilgrimage", "Ibrahim is told to call people to hajj. It is not the meat or blood of the sacrifice that reaches Allah, but your God-consciousness (26–37)."],
    ["shield", "Permission to defend", "Those who were wronged and driven from their homes are allowed to fight back (39–41)."]],
  23: ["Who are the successful believers?",
    ["heart", "The successful", "Those humble in prayer, who avoid idle talk, give zakah, guard their chastity, keep their trusts and their prayers — they will inherit Paradise (1–11)."],
    ["drop", "How we are made", "From clay, then a drop, a clinging clot, a lump, bones clothed with flesh — ‘so blessed is Allah, the best of creators’ (12–16)."],
    ["ship", "Nuh and those after him", "Nuh, then other messengers, Musa and Harun, and ‘Isa and his mother (23–50)."],
    ["scales", "No going back", "At death a person begs to return and do good, but it is only a word he says (99–115)."]],
  24: ["Light for the home and society: modesty, honesty and the famous Verse of Light.",
    ["scales", "Guarding honour", "Rules about chastity and false accusation; the slander against ‘A’ishah is exposed and she is declared innocent (1–26)."],
    ["house", "Manners of the home", "Ask permission before entering houses, lower the gaze, and dress modestly (27–31, 58–61)."],
    ["lamp", "The Verse of Light", "Allah is the Light of the heavens and the earth. His light is like a niche with a lamp in glass like a shining star, lit from a blessed olive tree — light upon light (35)."],
    ["night", "Darkness upon darkness", "The deeds of deniers are like a mirage in the desert, or like layers of darkness in a deep sea (39–40)."]],
  25: ["The Criterion between right and wrong, ending with a portrait of Allah’s true servants.",
    ["book", "The Criterion", "Objections to the Messenger and the Quran are answered. On the Last Day the Messenger will say, ‘My Lord, my people abandoned this Quran’ (1–34)."],
    ["sky", "Signs", "The stretching shadow, night as a covering, winds bringing rain, and two seas — one sweet, one salty — that do not mix (45–62)."],
    ["heart", "Servants of the Most Merciful", "They walk humbly, answer the ignorant with peace, pray at night, spend in moderation, and repent (63–77)."]],
  26: ["Prophet after prophet says the same words: ‘I ask you for no reward.’",
    ["staff", "Musa and Pharaoh", "Musa strikes the sea and it parts, each side like a great mountain (10–68)."],
    ["fire", "Ibrahim", "He asks his people about their idols and makes a beautiful prayer to the Lord who feeds, heals and forgives (69–104)."],
    ["ruins", "Five peoples", "The peoples of Nuh, Hud, Salih, Lut and Shu‘ayb all rejected their messengers (105–191)."],
    ["pen", "Revelation, not poetry", "The Quran was brought down by the Trustworthy Spirit; it is not the word of poets who wander in every valley (192–227)."]],
  27: ["The kingdom of Sulayman and the Queen of Saba’.",
    ["fire", "Musa at the fire", "Musa is called at the fire and given nine signs for Pharaoh (7–14)."],
    ["throne", "Sulayman and the valley of ants", "Sulayman understands the speech of birds. As his army approaches, an ant warns the others; he smiles and thanks Allah (15–19)."],
    ["scroll", "The letter to the queen", "The hoopoe brings news of a queen who worships the sun. Sulayman sends a letter beginning ‘In the name of Allah’ (20–37)."],
    ["throne", "The throne and the glass palace", "Her throne is brought in the blink of an eye. She enters a palace of glass and says, ‘I submit with Sulayman to Allah, Lord of the worlds’ (38–44)."],
    ["ruins", "Salih and Lut", "Nine men plot against Salih; Lut’s people are destroyed (45–58)."]],
  28: ["The life of Musa from birth, and the fall of the arrogant.",
    ["river", "The baby in the river", "Musa’s mother places him in the river. Pharaoh’s family takes him in, and Allah returns him to his mother (3–13)."],
    ["well", "The well of Madyan", "Musa flees Egypt, waters the flock for two women at a well, prays ‘My Lord, I am in need of whatever good You send me,’ and is given a home and marriage (14–28)."],
    ["fire", "The call", "On his way back he sees a fire and is made a messenger (29–35)."],
    ["sea", "Pharaoh’s end", "Pharaoh and his armies are thrown into the sea (36–42)."],
    ["coins", "Qarun", "Qarun was so rich that his keys were heavy for strong men. He boasted, and the earth swallowed him and his house (76–82)."]],
  29: ["Faith will be tested. Do not lean on what is weak.",
    ["heart", "The test", "‘Do people think they will be left alone because they say “We believe” and will not be tested?’ (2–3)."],
    ["ship", "Prophets who were tested", "Nuh stayed among his people for a thousand years less fifty; Ibrahim, Lut and others are remembered (14–40)."],
    ["web", "The spider’s house", "Those who take protectors other than Allah are like the spider that builds a house — the weakest of all houses (41)."],
    ["book", "Recite and pray", "Recite the Book and establish prayer; prayer keeps one away from indecency and wrong (45)."]],
  30: ["A prophecy that came true, and signs of Allah in everyday life.",
    ["shield", "The Romans", "The Romans have been defeated, but within a few years they will win — and they did (1–6)."],
    ["heart", "His signs", "He created you from dust; made spouses for you with love and mercy between you; the variety of your languages and colours; your sleep; lightning and rain (20–25)."],
    ["wind", "Winds and revival", "He sends winds that raise the clouds, and gives life to the earth after it was dead — so will He raise the dead (46–50)."]],
  31: ["The wise advice of Luqman to his son.",
    ["tree", "Luqman’s advice", "Do not associate anything with Allah. Be good to parents. Allah knows even a mustard seed inside a rock. Pray, be patient, do not be proud, walk gently and lower your voice (12–19)."],
    ["sky", "Signs and the unseen", "If all trees were pens and the sea ink, the words of Allah would not run out. Five things only Allah knows (27, 34)."]],
  32: ["From creation to the return — and the believers who bow down.",
    ["drop", "The creation of man", "He began man from clay, then shaped him and breathed His spirit into him (4–9)."],
    ["heart", "Those who prostrate", "Their sides leave their beds to call on their Lord in fear and hope. No soul knows what joy is kept hidden for it (15–17)."]],
  33: ["The battle of the Trench, and guidance for the Prophet’s household.",
    ["shield", "The Trench", "Allied armies surround Madinah. The believers stand firm, and Allah sends a wind and unseen forces (9–27)."],
    ["house", "The Prophet’s family", "His wives are the mothers of the believers. Adopted sons keep their own fathers’ names. Muhammad ﷺ is the Messenger of Allah and the seal of the prophets (4–6, 28–40)."],
    ["heart", "Blessings on the Prophet", "Allah and His angels send blessings on the Prophet; believers are told to do the same, and the rule of modest dress follows soon after (56, 59)."],
    ["mountain", "The Trust", "The Trust was offered to the heavens, the earth and the mountains; they declined it, and man took it on (72)."]],
  34: ["Gratitude kept and gratitude lost.",
    ["throne", "Dawud and Sulayman", "Mountains and birds glorify with Dawud, and iron is made soft for him. The wind and the jinn serve Sulayman; his death is shown only when a creature eats his staff (10–14)."],
    ["garden", "The people of Saba’", "They had two gardens and a forgiving Lord, but were ungrateful. The flood of the dam swept it away (15–19)."]],
  35: ["Allah is the Originator; all honour and power belong to Him.",
    ["sky", "The Originator", "He made angels messengers with wings. Whatever mercy He opens, none can hold back (1–3)."],
    ["rain", "Colours of creation", "Fruits, mountains, people and animals of many colours. Those who truly fear Allah are the ones with knowledge (27–28)."],
    ["book", "Heirs of the Book", "Some wrong themselves, some take a middle course, and some race ahead in good deeds (32)."]],
  36: ["Often called the heart of the Quran: the message, the signs, and the resurrection.",
    ["house", "The people of the town", "Three messengers come to a town. A man runs from the far side of the city saying, ‘O my people, follow the messengers’ (13–29)."],
    ["sprout", "Signs", "The dead earth brought to life, night and day, the sun and moon each floating in an orbit, and the loaded ship (33–44)."],
    ["trumpet", "The Trumpet", "The Trumpet is blown and people rise from their graves. Mouths are sealed, and hands and feet speak (51–65)."],
    ["drop", "Be, and it is", "Man asks, ‘Who can give life to bones?’ The One who made them the first time. His command is only ‘Be,’ and it is (77–83)."]],
  37: ["The angels in ranks, and the trials of the prophets.",
    ["sky", "Those in ranks", "Angels standing in rows; the nearest heaven adorned with stars (1–10)."],
    ["fire", "Ibrahim’s sacrifice", "He breaks the idols and is saved from the fire. Then he sees in a dream that he must sacrifice his son; both submit, and Allah ransoms him with a great sacrifice (83–111)."],
    ["ship", "Yunus", "He leaves on a loaded ship, is cast out and swallowed by a great fish, and is saved because he glorified Allah; a gourd plant shades him (139–148)."],
    ["book", "Peace upon the messengers", "Nuh, Musa and Harun, Ilyas and Lut are each greeted with peace (75–138)."]],
  38: ["Prophets who turned back to Allah, and the pride of Iblis.",
    ["throne", "Dawud and Sulayman", "Two men climb into Dawud’s chamber with a dispute, and he learns to judge with care. Sulayman is given a kingdom, the wind and the jinn (17–40)."],
    ["river", "Ayyub", "In his suffering he calls his Lord; he is told to strike the ground and a cool spring appears (41–44)."],
    ["garden", "Iblis’s pride", "‘I am better than him: You made me from fire and him from clay’ (71–85)."]],
  39: ["Worship Allah sincerely — and never lose hope in His mercy.",
    ["heart", "Do not despair", "‘O My servants who have wronged themselves, do not despair of the mercy of Allah. Allah forgives all sins’ (53)."],
    ["trumpet", "The crowds", "The Trumpet is blown twice. The deniers are driven to Hell in crowds, and the God-conscious are led to Paradise in crowds (68–75)."]],
  40: ["The Forgiver — and a believer who spoke the truth in Pharaoh’s court.",
    ["heart", "Forgiver of sin", "The angels who carry the Throne pray for the believers (1–9). ‘Call upon Me; I will answer you’ (60)."],
    ["staff", "The believer of Pharaoh’s family", "A man who hid his faith stands up: ‘Would you kill a man because he says, My Lord is Allah?’ Allah protects him (28–45)."]],
  41: ["The Quran explained clearly, and the best way to answer hostility.",
    ["sky", "Creation", "The earth, its mountains and provisions, then the heavens, all made in days (9–12)."],
    ["wind", "‘Ad and Thamud", "A furious wind for ‘Ad and a blast for Thamud. On the Last Day ears, eyes and skins will testify (13–24)."],
    ["heart", "Answer with what is better", "Angels come down on those who say ‘Our Lord is Allah’ and stay firm. Repel evil with good, and your enemy may become a close friend (30–35)."]],
  42: ["One religion for all the prophets, and decisions made by consultation.",
    ["book", "One religion", "The same way was given to Nuh, Ibrahim, Musa and ‘Isa: establish the religion and do not divide. Nothing is like Him (11–13)."],
    ["scales", "Consultation and forgiveness", "Believers decide their affairs by consulting each other; whoever forgives and makes peace, his reward is with Allah (36–43)."],
    ["ship", "Ships like mountains", "Among His signs are the ships sailing on the sea; if He willed He could still the wind (32–34)."]],
  43: ["Gold and glitter are only the enjoyment of this life.",
    ["coins", "The value of wealth", "If it would not make all people disbelievers, Allah would have given the deniers roofs and stairs of silver. All of that is only worldly enjoyment (33–35)."],
    ["staff", "Musa and Pharaoh", "Pharaoh boasts, ‘Is the kingdom of Egypt not mine, and these rivers flowing beneath me?’ (46–56)."],
    ["book", "‘Isa", "‘Isa was only a servant whom Allah blessed and made an example (57–65)."]],
  44: ["A blessed night, and the end of the proud.",
    ["night", "The blessed night", "The Book was sent down on a blessed night in which every wise matter is decided (1–6)."],
    ["sea", "What Pharaoh’s people left behind", "How many gardens, springs and fields they left! Neither sky nor earth wept for them (17–33)."],
    ["garden", "Two ends", "The tree of Zaqqum for the sinful; gardens and springs for the God-conscious (43–57)."]],
  45: ["Signs for those who think, and every nation on its knees.",
    ["sky", "Signs", "In the heavens and earth, in your own creation, in rain and wind. The sea is made to serve you (1–13)."],
    ["scales", "Kneeling", "You will see every nation kneeling, each called to its record (27–29)."]],
  46: ["Goodness to parents, the fate of ‘Ad, and jinn who listened.",
    ["heart", "Parents", "His mother carried him with hardship; at forty he prays, ‘My Lord, help me to thank You for Your favour on me and my parents’ (15)."],
    ["wind", "The sand-dunes", "‘Ad saw a cloud coming and said, ‘This will bring us rain.’ It was a wind carrying punishment (21–26)."],
    ["book", "The jinn listen", "A group of jinn hear the Quran, say ‘Be silent,’ and go back to warn their people (29–32)."]],
  47: ["Believers and deniers compared.",
    ["shield", "Struggle", "Rules of fighting; if you help Allah’s cause He will help you and make your feet firm (4–7)."],
    ["river", "The rivers of Paradise", "Rivers of water, milk, wine that brings no harm, and pure honey (15)."],
    ["heart", "Reflect", "‘Do they not reflect on the Quran, or are there locks upon their hearts?’ (24)."]],
  48: ["The peace treaty of Hudaybiyyah — a clear victory.",
    ["scroll", "A clear victory", "‘We have given you a clear victory’ — revealed after the treaty (1–3)."],
    ["tree", "The pledge under the tree", "Allah was pleased with the believers when they pledged to you under the tree, and sent calm upon them (18)."],
    ["kaaba", "The vision fulfilled", "You will enter the Sacred Mosque in safety. The believers are like a seed that sends out its shoot and grows strong (27–29)."]],
  49: ["Manners that hold a community together.",
    ["house", "Respect", "Do not raise your voices above the voice of the Prophet or call out from behind the rooms (1–5)."],
    ["scales", "Check and reconcile", "Verify news before acting on it. If two groups of believers fight, make peace between them; believers are brothers (6–10)."],
    ["heart", "Guard the tongue", "No mocking, no insulting nicknames, no suspicion, no spying, no backbiting (11–12)."],
    ["path", "One human family", "You were made into nations and tribes to know one another. The most noble of you is the most God-conscious (13)."]],
  50: ["Death, and the Day we come out of the graves.",
    ["sprout", "Rain and revival", "Blessed rain brings gardens and grain to life from dead land — ‘so will be the coming out’ (6–11)."],
    ["heart", "Nearer than the jugular vein", "Allah knows what the soul whispers. Two angels record every word (16–18)."],
    ["trumpet", "The Day", "The daze of death comes with truth; the Trumpet is blown; Hell is asked, ‘Are you full?’ (19–35)."]],
  51: ["Why were we created?",
    ["wind", "The scattering winds", "Oaths by the winds, the clouds and the ships: what you are promised is true (1–6)."],
    ["house", "Ibrahim’s guests", "Honoured guests bring news of a knowledgeable son (24–30)."],
    ["ruins", "Earlier peoples", "Lut’s people, Pharaoh, ‘Ad, Thamud and the people of Nuh (31–46)."],
    ["heart", "Our purpose", "‘I did not create jinn and humans except to worship Me’ (56)."]],
  52: ["An oath by the Mount that the punishment is certain.",
    ["mountain", "The oaths", "By the Mount, the written Book, the raised sky and the sea set on fire (1–8)."],
    ["garden", "Families together", "Believers are joined with their children who followed them in faith (17–28)."],
    ["book", "Questions for the deniers", "‘Were they created from nothing, or are they the creators?’ Be patient and glorify your Lord (29–49)."]],
  53: ["Revelation is true; everyone receives what he strove for.",
    ["sky", "The vision", "Your companion has not gone astray. He was taught by one mighty in power and saw him near the Lote Tree of the farthest limit (1–18)."],
    ["scales", "Only what you strive for", "The idols are only names. No one bears another’s burden, and a person will have only what he worked for (19–42)."]],
  54: ["A repeated question: the Quran is made easy to remember — will anyone remember?",
    ["moon", "The moon split", "The Hour has drawn near and the moon has split (1–2)."],
    ["ship", "Nuh", "Nuh calls, ‘I am overpowered, so help.’ The sky pours and the earth gushes; he is carried on planks and nails (9–15)."],
    ["wind", "‘Ad, Thamud, Lut and Pharaoh", "A screaming wind, the blast, a storm of stones, and the drowning (18–42)."],
    ["book", "Made easy", "‘We have certainly made the Quran easy to remember. So is there anyone who will remember?’ — repeated four times."]],
  55: ["The Most Merciful and His favours. One question returns again and again: ‘Which of your Lord’s favours will you deny?’",
    ["sky", "Favours on earth", "He taught the Quran, created man, set the sun and moon on their courses, raised the sky and set up the balance (1–13)."],
    ["sea", "The two seas", "Two seas meet with a barrier between them; from them come pearls and coral, and ships like mountains (19–25)."],
    ["garden", "The gardens", "For the one who feared standing before his Lord there are two gardens, with springs and fruit — and two more besides (46–78)."]],
  56: ["The Event that cannot be denied, and the three groups of people.",
    ["quake", "The Event", "The earth is shaken and the mountains crumble to dust (1–6)."],
    ["garden", "Three groups", "The foremost who are brought near, the people of the right, and the people of the left (7–56)."],
    ["sprout", "Think", "The seed you sow, the water you drink, the fire you light — did you make them, or did We? (57–74)."],
    ["book", "A noble Quran", "In a well-guarded Book, touched only by the purified (75–80)."]],
  57: ["Faith that gives: spend, soften your heart, and keep this life in proportion.",
    ["coins", "Believe and spend", "Who will lend Allah a good loan, so that He multiplies it? (7–11)."],
    ["lamp", "The light of the believers", "Their light runs ahead of them. The hypocrites beg, ‘Wait for us,’ and a wall is set between them (12–15)."],
    ["rain", "This life", "It is like rain whose plants please the farmer, then turn yellow and crumble (20)."],
    ["shield", "Iron", "Messengers came with the Book and the balance, and iron was sent down with great strength and benefits (25)."]],
  58: ["Allah hears every plea and every secret talk.",
    ["house", "The woman who pleaded", "Allah heard the woman who complained about her husband’s unjust words, and gave a ruling (1–4)."],
    ["heart", "Secret talk and gatherings", "No three speak in secret but He is the fourth. Make room for each other in gatherings (7–11)."]],
  59: ["The exile of a tribe that broke its treaty, and the beautiful names of Allah.",
    ["ruins", "The exile", "Banu Nadir thought their forts would protect them; they left their homes (2–6)."],
    ["coins", "Giving and preferring others", "The Ansar love those who came to them and prefer them over themselves, even when in need (7–10)."],
    ["mountain", "If it came down on a mountain", "A mountain would humble itself and split from awe of Allah. Then come His names: the King, the Holy, the Peace… (21–24)."]],
  60: ["Loyalty and fairness.",
    ["heart", "Loyalty", "Do not take those who fight your faith as close allies; Ibrahim is the example (1–6)."],
    ["scales", "Fairness to the peaceful", "Allah does not forbid you from being kind and just to those who did not fight you (8)."],
    ["scroll", "The women who emigrated", "Believing women who emigrate are tested and give their pledge (10–12)."]],
  61: ["Let your deeds match your words.",
    ["shield", "A solid row", "‘Why do you say what you do not do?’ Allah loves those who stand in ranks like a firm building (2–4)."],
    ["book", "‘Isa’s good news", "‘Isa tells of a messenger to come after him whose name is Ahmad (6)."],
    ["coins", "A trade that saves", "Believe and strive with your wealth and your lives (10–13)."]],
  62: ["Knowledge must be lived, and Friday prayer comes before trade.",
    ["book", "The Messenger and the Book", "A messenger was sent to teach the Book and wisdom. Those who carry the Torah without acting on it are like one loaded with books he does not understand (2–5)."],
    ["mosque", "Friday", "When the call is made for Friday prayer, hurry to the remembrance of Allah and leave trade; afterwards spread out and seek His bounty (9–11)."]],
  63: ["How to recognise hypocrisy.",
    ["heart", "The hypocrites", "Their looks and words impress, but they use their oaths as a cover (1–8)."],
    ["coins", "Before death comes", "Do not let wealth and children distract you from remembering Allah; spend before you say, ‘My Lord, give me a little more time’ (9–11)."]],
  64: ["The Day when it becomes clear who really gained and who lost.",
    ["scales", "Gain and loss", "The Day of Gathering is the day of mutual loss and gain (9)."],
    ["heart", "Trust and trial", "No disaster strikes except by Allah’s permission. Wealth and children are a trial; be mindful of Allah as much as you can (11–16)."]],
  65: ["Divorce with fairness — and trust in Allah.",
    ["scales", "Rules of divorce", "The waiting period, housing and support (1–7)."],
    ["heart", "A way out", "Whoever is mindful of Allah, He makes a way out for him and provides from where he never expected (2–3)."]],
  66: ["Protect your family — and four women as examples.",
    ["house", "The Prophet’s household", "A private matter becomes a lesson. ‘Protect yourselves and your families from the Fire’; turn to Allah in sincere repentance (1–8)."],
    ["heart", "Four women", "The wives of Nuh and Lut did not benefit from their husbands. Pharaoh’s wife and Maryam are examples of faith (10–12)."]],
  67: ["The Kingdom belongs to Allah. A surah of protection, recited at night.",
    ["sky", "A flawless creation", "He created death and life to test you. Look at the seven heavens — look again; you will find no crack (1–5)."],
    ["fire", "The question", "The keepers ask, ‘Did no warner come to you?’ They answer, ‘If only we had listened’ (6–11)."],
    ["drop", "Who else?", "Who holds the birds in the air? If your water sank away, who would bring you flowing water? (19–30)."]],
  68: ["By the pen — great character, and a lesson about greed.",
    ["pen", "The pen", "By the pen and what they write: you are of great character (1–7)."],
    ["garden", "The owners of the garden", "They swore to pick their fruit early so that no poor person would get any. In the night it was burnt black (17–33)."],
    ["ship", "The man of the fish", "Be patient, and do not be like Yunus when he called out in distress (48–50)."]],
  69: ["The Reality that is sure to come.",
    ["wind", "Earlier nations", "Thamud by the blast; ‘Ad by a raging wind for seven nights and eight days; Pharaoh; and the flood (4–12)."],
    ["trumpet", "One blast", "The Trumpet is blown once; the earth and mountains are crushed (13–18)."],
    ["book", "The record", "One given his book in his right hand says, ‘Here, read my book!’ The other wishes he had never been given it (19–37)."]],
  70: ["Human restlessness, and its cure.",
    ["sky", "The Day", "A day whose length is fifty thousand years; the sky like molten metal and mountains like wool (1–18)."],
    ["heart", "The cure", "Man is anxious and tight-fisted — except those who are constant in prayer, share their wealth, and keep their trusts (19–35)."]],
  71: ["The patient call of Nuh.",
    ["ship", "Nuh’s call", "He calls his people night and day, openly and in private: ‘Seek forgiveness from your Lord — He will send rain, wealth and children.’ They hold on to their idols, and the flood comes (1–28)."]],
  72: ["The jinn hear the Quran.",
    ["sky", "The jinn listen", "A group of jinn say, ‘We have heard a wonderful recitation that guides to what is right, and we believe in it’ (1–15)."],
    ["mosque", "Places of prayer", "The mosques are for Allah alone, and He alone knows the unseen (18–28)."]],
  73: ["Stand in prayer at night and recite the Quran slowly and clearly.",
    ["night", "Night prayer", "O you wrapped in your cloak, stand through part of the night and recite the Quran in a measured way (1–9)."],
    ["staff", "Patience", "Bear what they say; Pharaoh disobeyed his messenger and was seized (10–19)."],
    ["book", "Ease", "Recite as much of it as is easy for you (20)."]],
  74: ["Arise and warn.",
    ["dawn", "Arise", "O you covered in your cloak, arise and warn, glorify your Lord, and purify your garments (1–7)."],
    ["fire", "Saqar", "One man thought, frowned and called the Quran magic. Over the Fire are nineteen keepers (11–31)."],
    ["heart", "What led you there?", "‘We were not of those who prayed, nor did we feed the poor’ (38–48)."]],
  75: ["The Resurrection, and the soul that blames itself.",
    ["trumpet", "That Day", "When sight is dazzled and the moon darkens, man asks, ‘Where can I flee?’ Allah can restore even his fingertips (1–15)."],
    ["book", "Do not hurry", "Do not move your tongue in haste; it is for Us to collect it and recite it (16–19)."],
    ["drop", "Left without purpose?", "Was he not a small drop, then shaped and formed? Can the One who did that not give life to the dead? (36–40)."]],
  76: ["The reward of those who feed others for Allah’s sake.",
    ["drop", "Tested", "Man was made from a mixed drop and shown the way — grateful or ungrateful (1–3)."],
    ["coins", "Feeding others", "They give food, though they love it, to the poor, the orphan and the captive: ‘We feed you only for the sake of Allah’ (5–10)."],
    ["garden", "Their reward", "Gardens, silk, shade and a spring called Salsabil (11–22)."]],
  77: ["‘Woe on that Day to the deniers’ — repeated ten times.",
    ["wind", "Those sent forth", "Oaths by the winds sent one after another (1–7)."],
    ["trumpet", "The Day of Sorting", "The stars are dimmed, the sky is split, the mountains are blown away (8–50)."]],
  78: ["The great news that people argue about.",
    ["sky", "Proofs in creation", "The earth as a bed, mountains as pegs, sleep for rest, the night as a covering, a blazing lamp, and rain from the clouds (6–16)."],
    ["trumpet", "The Day of Sorting", "The Trumpet is blown and you come in crowds (17–20)."],
    ["garden", "Two ends", "Hell lies in wait for the transgressors; for the God-conscious there are gardens and a full cup (21–40)."]],
  79: ["The Hour, and the story of Pharaoh in a few lines.",
    ["staff", "Musa and Pharaoh", "Pharaoh said, ‘I am your lord, most high,’ and Allah seized him (15–26)."],
    ["sky", "Which is harder?", "Are you harder to create, or the sky that He built? (27–33)."],
    ["quake", "The great overwhelming", "Whoever feared standing before his Lord and held back his soul from desire, Paradise is his home (34–46)."]],
  80: ["Every seeker matters.",
    ["heart", "He frowned", "A blind man came eagerly to learn while the Prophet ﷺ was speaking to leaders. Allah teaches that the one who comes seeking deserves attention (1–16)."],
    ["sprout", "Look at your food", "Rain poured down, the earth split, and grain, grapes, olives, dates and gardens grew (24–32)."],
    ["trumpet", "The deafening blast", "A man will flee from his brother, his mother, his father, his wife and his children (33–42)."]],
  81: ["When the sun is folded up.",
    ["sun", "The end of the world", "The sun is wrapped up, the stars fall, the mountains move, the seas boil — and the baby girl buried alive is asked for what sin she was killed (1–14)."],
    ["book", "The message is true", "This is the word of a noble messenger; it is a reminder to the worlds (15–29)."]],
  82: ["What deceived you about your generous Lord?",
    ["sky", "The sky breaks apart", "The stars scatter, the seas burst, and the graves are overturned (1–5)."],
    ["pen", "Noble recorders", "Over you are guardians, noble and writing, who know what you do (6–19)."]],
  83: ["Woe to those who cheat.",
    ["scales", "Cheating in measure", "They take full measure from people but give less when they measure for others (1–6)."],
    ["book", "Two records", "The record of the wicked is in Sijjin; the record of the righteous is in ‘Illiyyun (7–28)."],
    ["garden", "The last laugh", "Those who mocked the believers will be watched from couches in Paradise (29–36)."]],
  84: ["You are travelling towards your Lord.",
    ["sky", "The sky splits", "The sky and the earth obey their Lord (1–5)."],
    ["path", "The journey", "O human, you are toiling towards your Lord and you will meet Him (6)."],
    ["book", "The record", "One receives his record in his right hand and returns joyful; another receives it behind his back (7–15)."]],
  85: ["Believers who were burned for their faith.",
    ["fire", "The people of the trench", "They dug a trench of fire and sat watching what they did to the believers — only because they believed in Allah (4–10)."],
    ["sky", "A glorious Quran", "By the sky with its great stars: this is a glorious Quran in a Preserved Tablet (1, 21–22)."]],
  86: ["The night-comer.",
    ["sky", "The piercing star", "Every soul has a guardian over it (1–4)."],
    ["drop", "Look at your origin", "Man was created from a gushing fluid; Allah is able to bring him back (5–10)."],
    ["rain", "A decisive word", "By the sky that returns rain and the earth that splits open, this is a decisive word (11–17)."]],
  87: ["Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High.",
    ["sky", "The Most High", "He created and proportioned, measured and guided (1–5)."],
    ["book", "You will not forget", "‘We will make you recite, so you will not forget.’ The Hereafter is better and more lasting; this is in the scriptures of Ibrahim and Musa (6–19)."]],
  88: ["The overwhelming Day.",
    ["garden", "Two kinds of faces", "Faces humbled and worn out, and faces joyful in a high garden (1–16)."],
    ["mountain", "Look around you", "At the camels, how they are created; the sky, how it is raised; the mountains, how they are set; the earth, how it is spread (17–26)."]],
  89: ["By the dawn.",
    ["dawn", "The oaths", "By the dawn and the ten nights (1–5)."],
    ["ruins", "Three powers", "‘Ad of the lofty pillars, Thamud who carved the rocks, and Pharaoh — all were swept away (6–14)."],
    ["coins", "The test of wealth", "You do not honour the orphan, nor urge feeding the poor, and you love wealth too much (15–20)."],
    ["heart", "The soul at peace", "‘O soul at peace, return to your Lord, pleased and pleasing. Enter among My servants; enter My Paradise’ (27–30)."]],
  90: ["The steep path.",
    ["kaaba", "This city", "An oath by Makkah: man was created to face hardship (1–10)."],
    ["mountain", "The steep path", "Freeing a slave, or feeding an orphan relative or a poor person on a day of hunger, with patience and mercy (11–20)."]],
  91: ["Purify the soul.",
    ["sun", "Seven oaths", "By the sun, the moon, the day, the night, the sky, the earth and the soul: successful is the one who purifies it (1–10)."],
    ["ruins", "Thamud", "They killed the she-camel, and their Lord destroyed them for their sin (11–15)."]],
  92: ["Two roads.",
    ["night", "Night and day", "Your efforts are of different kinds (1–4)."],
    ["coins", "The giver and the miser", "Whoever gives and is mindful of Allah is eased towards ease; whoever is miserly is eased towards hardship (5–21)."]],
  93: ["Comfort for the Prophet ﷺ after revelation paused.",
    ["dawn", "You are not forsaken", "Your Lord has not left you, nor is He displeased. What comes later is better for you than what came before (1–5)."],
    ["heart", "So be kind", "He found you an orphan and sheltered you. So do not be harsh with the orphan, do not turn away the one who asks, and speak of your Lord’s blessings (6–11)."]],
  94: ["With hardship comes ease.",
    ["heart", "Relief", "Did We not open your chest and lift your burden? With hardship comes ease — said twice. When you are free, turn to your Lord (1–8)."]],
  95: ["The best of forms.",
    ["mountain", "Four oaths", "By the fig, the olive, Mount Sinai and this safe city (1–3)."],
    ["heart", "High or low", "Man was created in the best form, then brought to the lowest — except those who believe and do good (4–8)."]],
  96: ["The first words revealed: ‘Read!’",
    ["pen", "Read", "Read in the name of your Lord who created — taught by the pen, taught man what he did not know (1–5)."],
    ["heart", "Prostrate and draw near", "Man oversteps when he thinks he needs no one. Do not obey the one who forbids prayer; prostrate and draw near (6–19)."]],
  97: ["The Night of Decree.",
    ["night", "Better than a thousand months", "The Quran was sent down on this night. The angels and the Spirit come down, and it is peace until dawn (1–5)."]],
  98: ["The clear proof.",
    ["book", "The clear proof", "A messenger reciting pure pages. People were told only to worship Allah sincerely, pray and give zakah (1–5)."],
    ["garden", "The best of creation", "Those who believe and do good: Allah is pleased with them and they with Him (6–8)."]],
  99: ["The earthquake.",
    ["quake", "The earth speaks", "The earth shakes, throws out its burdens and tells its news. Whoever does an atom’s weight of good will see it, and whoever does an atom’s weight of evil will see it (1–8)."]],
  100: ["Human ingratitude.",
    ["dawn", "The charge at dawn", "An oath by the chargers that run panting, strike sparks and raid at dawn (1–5)."],
    ["coins", "Ungrateful", "Man is ungrateful to his Lord and intense in his love of wealth. Does he not know what is in the graves will be brought out? (6–11)."]],
  101: ["The striking calamity.",
    ["scales", "The scales", "People will be like scattered moths and mountains like fluffed wool. Heavy scales bring a pleasant life; light scales, the pit (1–11)."]],
  102: ["Competing for more.",
    ["coins", "Distracted", "Rivalry in piling up distracts you until you visit the graves. Then you will be asked about every blessing (1–8)."]],
  103: ["The whole way of success in three verses.",
    ["sun", "By time", "Mankind is in loss — except those who believe, do good deeds, urge one another to truth, and urge one another to patience (1–3)."]],
  104: ["The slanderer.",
    ["coins", "Counting wealth", "Woe to every backbiter who gathers wealth and counts it, thinking it will make him live forever (1–3)."],
    ["fire", "The Crusher", "He will be thrown into the Fire of Allah that reaches the hearts (4–9)."]],
  105: ["The year of the elephant.",
    ["stones", "The army of the elephant", "An army came with an elephant to destroy the Ka‘bah. Allah sent flocks of birds that pelted them with stones of baked clay and left them like chewed straw (1–5)."]],
  106: ["Thankfulness for safety and food.",
    ["kaaba", "Quraysh", "For their safe journeys in winter and summer, let them worship the Lord of this House, who fed them against hunger and made them safe from fear (1–4)."]],
  107: ["Small kindnesses.",
    ["coins", "Denying the religion", "It is the one who pushes away the orphan and does not urge feeding the poor (1–3)."],
    ["mosque", "Empty prayer", "Woe to those careless of their prayer, who only show off and hold back even small help (4–7)."]],
  108: ["Abundance.",
    ["river", "Al-Kawthar", "We have given you abundance. So pray to your Lord and sacrifice. It is your enemy who is cut off (1–3)."]],
  109: ["Clear separation in worship.",
    ["path", "Two ways", "I do not worship what you worship, and you do not worship what I worship. To you your religion, and to me mine (1–6)."]],
  110: ["Victory and humility.",
    ["kaaba", "The help of Allah", "When victory comes and you see people entering Allah’s religion in crowds, glorify your Lord with praise and ask His forgiveness (1–3)."]],
  111: ["The end of an enemy.",
    ["rope", "Abu Lahab", "His wealth will not help him. He will enter a blazing fire, and his wife too, the carrier of firewood, with a rope of palm fibre round her neck (1–5)."]],
  112: ["Pure faith in One God.",
    ["sky", "Allah is One", "Say: He is Allah, the One; Allah, the Eternal on whom all depend. He did not beget, nor was He begotten, and there is none comparable to Him (1–4)."]],
  113: ["Seeking protection from outside harm.",
    ["dawn", "The Lord of daybreak", "I seek refuge from the evil of what He created, of the darkness when it settles, of those who blow on knots, and of the envier when he envies (1–5)."]],
  114: ["Seeking protection from the whisper within.",
    ["heart", "The Lord of mankind", "I seek refuge in the Lord, the King, the God of mankind, from the whisperer who withdraws, who whispers into people’s chests — from among jinn and men (1–6)."]]
};
